  "benefits_features_and_faqs": {
    "about_overview": "Standard Chartered Ultimate is a premium credit card offering **3.33% value-back** across multiple spending categories, matching top premium cards like **HDFC Diners Club Black** and **HDFC Infinia**. It also provides notable travel benefits, including **5% cashback on duty-free purchases** and a **low forex mark-up of 2%**. Up to **12 complimentary rounds annually** at premier golf courses in India further add to its benefits. However, the card falls short on **lounge access** , offering **12 free visits per year** with a **spend-based condition**. Additionally, its **lifestyle perks** in categories like **dining and entertainment** are limited. Despite lacking on additional benefits, the card’s core rewards program is strong. It stands out for its broad reward coverage, including utilities, insurance, and education—categories often excluded by other cards. If you are a high-spender and do not seek air mile conversion and prefer redemption through vouchers and merchandise, this card can be a great fit.",
    "highlights": [
      "5 reward points for every Rs. 150 spent",
      "3 reward points for every Rs. 150 spent on utilities, supermarkets, insurance, property management, schools & government payments",
      "Value of 1 reward point = Rs. 1 (redeemable through Standard Chartered Bank’s 360° rewards portal, against products and vouchers)",
      "6,000 bonus reward points worth Rs. 6,000 on card activation"
    ],
    "welcome_benefit": "Welcome benefit compensates for the joining fee",
